  "limits": "Receiver is a stand-in in a second database on the same local PostgreSQL server. Claim-fault cases gate a synchronous receiver-call marker; the existing separate receiver-database cases test effect deduplication. A client is killed before COMMIT and successful replies are withheld from a simulated worker: controlled fault injection, not a real network fault. No email/payment provider, broker, independent machine failure, real five-minute lease duration or latency measured. Lock-wait cases use observed one-second deadlines; other expiry is injected explicitly. Follow-ups authorise at a post-lock predicate test; a delayed commit need not precede the deadline. Retirement cannot recall a request already sent.",
